@startuml RestroVibes - Authentication Flow
!theme plain
title RestroVibes - Authentication & Session Management

actor User
participant "Frontend\n(React SPA)" as FE
participant "Express API" as API
participant "Auth Middleware" as Auth
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Nodemailer" as Mail

== REGISTRATION ==

User -> FE : Fill sign-up form\n(name, email, password, phone, role)
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/register
API -> API : Validate allowed roles:\n["client", "restaurateurs"]
API -> API : Hash password (bcrypt, 10 rounds)
API -> DB : UsersModel.create({ ... })
DB --> API : User created (id, role)
API -> API : Generate JWT access token (1h)\n+ refresh token (7d)
API --> FE : 201 { user, accessToken, refreshToken }
FE -> FE : Store tokens in sessionStorage

== LOGIN ==

User -> FE : Enter email + password + role
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/login\n{ email, password, role }
API -> DB : findOne({ email, role })
DB --> API : User found
API -> API : bcrypt.compare(password, hash)
API -> API : Generate JWT access (1h) + refresh (7d)
API --> FE : { accessToken, refreshToken, user }
FE -> FE : Store in sessionStorage\n+ redirect to role-specific dashboard

== TOKEN REFRESH (Auto-Intercepted) ==

FE -> API : Any request with expired access token
API --> FE : 401 Unauthorized
FE -> FE : Axios interceptor catches 401
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/refresh-token\n{ refreshToken }
API -> DB : Validate refresh token exists + not expired
DB --> API : Valid
API -> API : Generate new access + refresh tokens
API -> DB : Update refresh token in DB
API --> FE : { accessToken, refreshToken }
FE -> FE : Update sessionStorage
FE -> API : Retry original request with new token
API --> FE : 200 { data }

== LOGOUT ==

User -> FE : Click logout
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/logout\n{ refreshToken }
API -> DB : Delete/invalidate refresh token
API --> FE : 200 Logged out
FE -> FE : Clear sessionStorage\n+ redirect to login

== FORGOT PASSWORD ==

User -> FE : Enter email
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/forgot-password\n{ email }
API -> DB : Find user by email
API -> API : crypto.randomBytes(32) -> 64-char hex token
API -> API : Set expiry: now + 10 minutes
API -> DB : Store reset_token + reset_token_expiry
API -> Mail : sendPasswordReset(email, token)
note right of Mail : Dev mode: log to console\nProd mode: SMTP email\nwith reset link
Mail --> User : Email with reset link\n{FRONTEND_URL}/reset-password?token=...
API --> FE : 200 "If email exists, reset link sent"\n(prevents user enumeration)

== RESET PASSWORD ==

User -> FE : Click link -> Enter new password
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/reset-password\n{ token, password }
API -> DB : Find user where\ reset_token = token\nAND reset_token_expiry > NOW()
DB --> API : User found (token valid)
API -> API : Validate password >= 8 chars
API -> API : Hash new password (bcrypt)
API -> DB : Update password +\nclear reset_token & expiry
API --> FE : 200 Password reset successful

== RATE LIMITING (Forgot Password) ==

note over API,DB : In-memory Map tracks last request time per email\nProduction: 60-second cooldown between requests\nDev mode: cooldown skipped

@enduml
